---

<aside class="intro">
  <h2>A documentation Wayback Machine (powered by Plakar and Cloudflare R2)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Time-travel any page:</strong> Every version is a <a href="https://www.plakar.io/docs/main/explanations/how-plakar-works/">Plakar snapshot</a>. Pick a version chip to
      rebuild that page on demand.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Retrieved live from an encrypted backup:</strong> Older versions are <a href="https://www.plakar.io/docs/main/references/commands/plakar-restore/"
        >decrypted and restored</a
      > at request time. Watch the real <code>plakar</code> commands and timings in the panel on the right.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The whole site is captured:</strong> pages, images, PDFs, data files, and even the stylesheet all come from the <a
        href="https://www.plakar.io/docs/main/references/commands/plakar-backup/">snapshot</a
      >.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Durable &amp; offsite:</strong> The <a href="https://www.plakar.io/docs/main/integrations/s3/">encrypted store</a> syncs to Cloudflare R2. Snapshot the current docs or
      create a new version yourself from the panel on the right.
    </li>
  </ul>
</aside>
